{
  "$schema": "capability-authority/ui-capabilities@1",
  "why": [
    "The twenty-four product capabilities this programme BUILT a user surface",
    "for, each bound to the browser scenario that proves a real Chromium",
    "issued its request.",
    "",
    "It exists so that `BrowserVerifiedUiCapabilities` is a DERIVED number and",
    "not a count of whatever happened to run. Without the binding, a journey",
    "could be deleted and the total would simply get smaller; with it, the",
    "denominator is fixed by what was built and the numerator is fixed by what",
    "the Point-7 proof artifact actually recorded, so the two can disagree —",
    "which is the only way the gate can fail.",
    "",
    "A row here is NOT a claim that the capability works. It names where the",
    "capability lives and which scenario would have to have executed for it to",
    "be credited. The credit itself comes from",
    "`docs/architecture/point7-proven-scenarios.json`, written by the runner",
    "and re-derived by the closure gate.",
    "",
    "Adding a UI capability means adding a row AND a scenario. Adding a row",
    "alone lowers the verified fraction, which is the correct direction: the",
    "capability exists and has not been proven."
  ],
  "entries": [
